														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835784">
									

<p>Man, when I first discovered scp, i was awful at writing. At the best of times you'd get an incoherent mess that completely defied things such as tone, theme, plot, and grammar. Now, if I sit down and write a story, it will at least make sense grammatically.</p>
<p>I mean, in my head i can craft a coherent story, but ideas don't mean [REDACTED] to be honest, the biggest struggle I've faced when joining the scp community, (aside from biting the bullet and dealing with the garbage interface that is wikidot) has been coming up with an idea I'm ok with throwing into the kindling. By that, I mean an idea which i don't think i could expand upon further when i improve in skill.</p>
<p>It's difficult to find someone who shares my struggle. I don't suffer from a lack of ideas. I don't suffer from a lack of effort. I struggle from being to picky. I have a plethora of ideas I wish to spew upon paper, but I just don't feel I'm sufficiently skilled enough to do them justice.</p>
<p>And I'm stuck in this purgatory of coming up with an idea that I'm ok with letting go of. I have so many ideas for scp as a whole, not just anomalous objects, I'm talking tales, GOI's, canons, and so much more. I guess I'm just frustrated that I'm not confident enough in my skull to allow myself to write what I want.</p>

