			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835770">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A sentient, living shadow, who belongs to a man named Clarence.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> It revolves around the wholesome relationship between Clarence and his Shadow.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I'm unsure if these listed below make the SCP unique on the site, but I hope this is what you meant by Hook or Attention Grabber. Just yell out if you want me to edit this.</p>
<ol>
<li>It's a sentient shadow (Most Shadow related SCPs I've researched have limited sentience or are just furniture)</li>
<li>It's unclear on whether Clarence is anomaly, the shadow, or just both.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;The&nbsp;Friendly&nbsp;Shadow's&nbsp;Quirk&nbsp;Ideas</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Whether these are a good ideas or not is why I'm putting these here. Yell out if any seem good or bad. I always like to hear feedback and opinions.</p>
<ol>
<li>I was thinking that the shadow could move off of Clarence and interact with other shadows of people and objects.</li>
<li>The shadow can talk to Clarence and others telepathically</li>
<li>The shadow can only talk to Clarence</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Expanding&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>As you probably saw above, I'm hoping to let this be emotional. I want a rather wholesome attachment with Clarence and his shadow. They have known of each other since childhood. It's not some recent anomaly. Below are a few extra ideas which I would like critique for. I was planning on doing one, but decided to keep my options open for the critters who have been doing this much longer then myself.</p>
<ol>
<li>The shadow is a parasite and is detrimental to Charles's health whether either of them know or not.</li>
<li>Forces wish for the shadow to leave Clarence and both protest.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;The&nbsp;Inspiration</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>For those who are as nerdy as me, the inspiration behind this was three things specifically.</p>
<ol>
<li>The Movie which has yet to (or may never) be released, Me and My Shadow. Note: If you've seen or are about to look up what this is, you'll know this had the biggest impact of the three.</li>
<li>Peter Pan and his shadow</li>
<li>Doctor Who, Season 4, Episode 8, Silence in the Library.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Let me know what can be used (if anything can be). Can't wait to hear from you. -Cope</p>

							</div>

								
					
