														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835758">
									

<p>So, like others have said before (above) the anomaly seems intended to make this person hard to contain. Which isn't super believable, as it seems like a gimmick to make it more dramatic.</p>
<p>Additionally, I don't understand why the Foundation would hire him at all. Or why they wouldn't just amnesticize him concerning the ability and his history with Chicago Spirit, then give him another identity and put him under surveillance.</p>
<p>Moreover, if they decided to contain him they could go in nontraditional methods: keeping him in a medically induced coma, containing him outdoors after amnesticizing him so that he lived a rural life on a farm somewhere or a mountain cabin and having him surveilled, or trying SRA's to negate his anomalous ability (as you mentioned they originated from his contact with something reality bending).</p>
<p>Finally, even if none of the above was effective or was just forgotten about for the moment&#8230; I don't know why the Foundation would consistently bail him out for bad petty crimes he tries to commit on the side&#8230; or even WHY he was trying to do so.</p>

							</div>

								
					
