			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835755">
									

<p>As a general note, minutiae information like containment chamber size (which unless it's rather pertinent to containment success, isn't a requirement by any means) or height (which can vary over time anyway) tend to not be aspects that will change a reader's vote. It can be good to have to help a reader better visualize the anomaly and containment, but the author should also be mindful of not getting bogged down in excessive specifics.</p>

